% The Drowned Knight (hazard terrain and physics objects)
%
% A knight in full plate holds a keep on a spit of rock. On one side the
% keep drops into a moat (a chasm); below the quay wall lies a deep lake.
% Nobody can hurt the knight: the terrain can. Its plate is the puzzle - it
% is heavy: nothing pushes or pulls it, and it would drag the knight to the
% bottom of the lake. Two companions, one skill each, from six.
%
%   gate --- quay --- causeway --- keep (knight) --- moat
%    |        :                      :
%   tower    lake (below the wall; no way down but a fall)
%
% Two ways, opposite in kind:
%   drown it   keep it heavy and make the knight move itself: taunted, it
%              leaps at its taunter (a dash, which no plate stops). Someone
%              has to be down in the lake first - put there by a friend:
%              washed off the quay (tidalWave), blasted off it (fireball),
%              or sucked down into the water (vortex on the lake) - and taunt
%              from the water. The knight leaps in after them and sinks.
%   drop it    turn it to mist (turnToMist): for a moment it is not heavy,
%              and the very next cast can move it - push it off the keep into
%              the moat from the causeway (fireball, tidalWave), suck it into
%              the moat (vortex), or pull it across the moat from the tower
%              (hook, taunt).
% Traps: misted, it no longer drowns (and the mist lasts one cast only); a
% knight taunted from dry land just leaps over to you (a leap never falls);
% hooked while heavy, it drags you onto the keep instead; nobody can walk
% down to the water (the quay wall is a door that never opens).
region(gate).
region(quay).
region(lake).
region(causeway).
region(keep).
region(moat).
region(tower).
connected(gate, quay).
connected(quay, gate).
connected(quay, causeway).
connected(causeway, quay).
connected(causeway, keep).
connected(keep, causeway).
connected(gate, tower).
connected(tower, gate).
% The lake lies below the quay and the moat below the keep: next to them
% (a vortex draws from there), but no way down on foot - the moat is a
% chasm, and the quay wall is a door that never opens.
connected(quay, lake).
connected(lake, quay).
connected(keep, moat).
connected(moat, keep).
door(lake).
lineOfSight(gate, quay).
lineOfSight(gate, lake).
lineOfSight(causeway, keep).
lineOfSight(causeway, moat).
lineOfSight(tower, keep).
lineOfSight(tower, moat).
lineOfSight(lake, keep).

% Push lines (and what lies between): from the gate, whoever stands on the
% quay goes over the wall into the lake; from the causeway, the keep's
% occupant goes into the moat; a pull from the tower crosses the moat.
beyond(gate, quay, lake).
beyond(causeway, keep, moat).
beyond(tower, moat, keep).

% === Terrain ===
onEnter(lake, deepWater).
onEnter(moat, chasm).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, gate).
at(mage, gate).
mana(player, 2).
mana(mage, 2).

% === The knight ===
% Heavy: no push or pull moves it, and the catalogue sinks the heavy in deep
% water. Taunted, it leaps at whoever did it (a dash).
role(knight, enemy).
at(knight, keep).
tag(knight, living).
tag(knight, heavy).
blocker(knight).
behavior(knight, taunted, lunge, source).
effect(lunge, target, dash).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, tidalWave).
knows(mage, taunt).

% === Victory ===
win :- if(), do(neutralize(knight), standing()).
win :- if(), do(bait(knight), standing()).

% Bait: a companion gets into water that drowns ?e, then provokes it from
% there, and ?e leaps in after them.
bait(?e) :-
    if(behavior(?e, ?t, lunge, source), onEnter(?r, ?z), effect(?z, target, hazard(?h)),
       weakness(?e, ?h, none, ?out), stops(?e, ?out), receptive(?e, ?h), canAct(?b),
       first(canInflict(?b, ?ab, ?t, ?e))),
    do(getInto(?b, ?r), inflictAs(?b, ?t, ?e), confirmStopped(?e)).

% ?b ends up in ?r, sent there by someone else from the side of the water.
getInto(?b, ?r) :- if(at(?b, ?r)), do().
getInto(?b, ?r) :-
    if(not(at(?b, ?r)), landing(?from, ?over, ?r)),
    do(walkTo(?b, ?over), place(?b, ?r, ?b), confirmAt(?b, ?r)).
confirmAt(?x, ?r) :- if(at(?x, ?r)), do().

% Nobody the team needs is lost on the way.
standing() :- if(not(first(and(canAct(?a), gone(?a))))), do().

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from six (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(turnToMist).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(hook).
comboMinWins(10).
comboMinMethods(4).

goals(win).
